  "notes": "A Russian teen duo rebuilt for the West as industrial-tinged Eurodance-rock: about 90 straight with a 16th-note industrial pulse and the backbeat on 2&4. Three drum facts are quoted and all three are authored — \"hard gated kick on 1 and 3&\" (anchor 1 with the second anchor on \"3&\"), \"distorted snare/clap on 2&4\" (the highest accent tier here with the clap offset tightened to zero), and \"16th noise-hat, plus a reversed-cymbal riser\", which is the pinned 16th base at a high fill density and the reverse/riser perc block. The harmony is F minor running i–VI–III–VII \"with a static tonic pedal\", which is why the harmonic rhythm leans to two bars a chord. The vocal fact is the one that shapes the melody most: both voices are \"confined to F4–D♭5, a deliberately narrow fifth-wide band, which is why the harmony is mostly parallel\" — the register is exactly that band and the counter runs octave-echo. The two live instruments are piano and electric guitar, so the bass is \"distorted saw bass in 8ths doubling the piano's left hand; heavily compressed, no slides\": `independent_riff` at 0.9 with `glideProb` 0. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and the melody density.",
